examples.question_text:
Find $x$. The angles lie on a straight line.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\draw (-2.3,0)--(2.3,0);
\draw (0,0)--(112:2);
\draw (0.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=112,radius=0.6];
\draw (112:0.85) arc[start angle=112,end angle=180,radius=0.85];
\node at (56:1.05) {$112^{\circ}$};
\node at (146:1.2) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Find $y$. The three adjacent angles fill one side of a straight line.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\draw (-2.4,0)--(2.4,0);
\draw (0,0)--(32.5:2.1);
\draw (0,0)--(79.25:2.1);
\draw (0.7,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=32.5,radius=0.7];
\draw (32.5:0.85) arc[start angle=32.5,end angle=79.25,radius=0.85];
\draw (79.25:0.65) arc[start angle=79.25,end angle=180,radius=0.65];
\node at (16.25:1.35) {$32.5^{\circ}$};
\node at (55.875:1.5) {$46.75^{\circ}$};
\node at (129.625:1.05) {$y$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

